; Example: Countdown loop in SUBLEQ (semantics/subleq-spec.md)
; x = 3
; while true:
;     output x
;     x = x - 1
;     if x <= 0: halt
;
; The previous version of this file put the data cells at address 0, so
; execution started inside the data and looped forever. Code now starts
; at address 0 and the data lives after the code.
;
; Addr | A  B  C  | Meaning
;  0   | 12 -1 3  | [OUT]   output X (b < 0 is output), go to 3
;  3   | 13 12 9  | [DEC]   X = X - ONE; if X <= 0 go to 9
;  6   | 14 14 0  | [JUMP]  Z = Z - Z = 0, so always go to 0
;  9   | 14 14 -1 | [HALT]  c = -1 halts
; 12   | 3        | X
; 13   | 1        | ONE
; 14   | 0        | Z
;
; Output: 3 2 1. Halts after 9 steps with PC = -1 and X = 0.
; This image is also the fixture "countdown-example" in
; verification/fixtures/edge-cases.json.

; Full memory image starting at 0:
12 -1 3  13 12 9  14 14 0  14 14 -1  3 1 0
